# core .so  ->  Buildroot symbol
#
# es_systems.yml gates every libretro core on a "BR2_PACKAGE_LIBRETRO_*"
# symbol.  Those symbols are no longer set: the cores come from the drop, and
# BR2_PACKAGE_KNULLI_EXTERNAL_LIBRETRO_CORES switches every "select" off.  This
# table is how the symbols come back -- gen-es-config.sh emits "<symbol>=y" for
# each row whose .so is actually in the drop, and knulli-es-system reads that
# alongside .config.  So es_systems.yml keeps working unmodified, and a system
# appears in EmulationStation exactly when a core for it is on the device.
#
# Rows were derived from the libretro-* Buildroot packages themselves (each
# package's Config.in symbol paired with the .so its .mk installs), so a symbol
# here means the same core it meant before the rework.  Rows for cores no drop
# builds are harmless; add a row when a core new to libretro-super needs to be
# reachable from es_systems.yml.
#
81_libretro.so                        BR2_PACKAGE_LIBRETRO_81
a5200_libretro.so                     BR2_PACKAGE_LIBRETRO_A5200
arduous_libretro.so                   BR2_PACKAGE_LIBRETRO_ARDUOUS
